                <pb facs="0513" n="423" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg423"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.85/1214½: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wallace</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-08-31T15:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 31,
                                1920—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>1423. B–100. For Boyden.</p>
                <p>Your B–200, August 13.</p>
                <p>Department approves your position. Emphasize that valuation of ships is under
                    jurisdiction of Reparation Commission and that Germany must receive full credit
                    for value of ships as of date when delivered to Allies.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
